-- #2722: a constrained standalone shadowing an imported method of the same name.
--
-- Two bindings of one bare name, in two different modules, and each occurrence has
-- exactly one right denotation.  Here in the entry module `size` denotes the imported
-- METHOD, so `size (Box 3)` is 3.  Inside `lib/shadow2722_shadow.mdk` the same bare
-- name denotes that module's OWN standalone, so `useIt 3` is `3 + 1`.  The program
-- therefore prints 4, and the value pin carries as much of the claim as the verdict
-- does: 3 would mean the method won in the shadowing module too.
import lib.shadow2722_iface.{Sizeable, size, Box(..)}
import lib.shadow2722_shadow.{useIt}

main = println (useIt (size (Box 3)))
